cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use cloudseed in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "cloudseed: secure multi-cloud landing zones and a Kubernetes platform from one command"
abstract: >-
  cloudseed is an open-source command-line tool that builds secure landing zones on AWS, Google Cloud and Azure
  (network, NAT, hardened bastion, security baseline, remote state) and the same shape on local VMware Fusion or
  Workstation VMs with Terraform and Ansible. It adds private Kubernetes (EKS, GKE, AKS, RKE2, kubeadm), a catalog of
  platform components, disaster-recovery drills, chaos experiments, compliance scans, a FIPS 140 mode, a local web
  console, an MCP server and an agentic mode.
authors:
